Changelog: 04-11-2026 11:32:10

Release 2.0.1.

Changelog: 03-11-2026 22:27:51

Release 2.0.0.

Changelog: 03-11-2026 22:09:14

Added. Settings…, a window with Xenia's settings that matter for playing, in the app (owner, 03-11-2026, from the
Windows Portable Suite's Xenia Manager; core's settings_page over xenia_settings): graphics (Vulkan, the Linux
build's), the resolution scale, anti-aliasing, scaling and sharpening, the picture's shape and VSync; the frame
limit and readback resolve; the sound output (SDL) and mute; the arcade license, achievement messages and the
guide button. Each is read from xenia-canary.config.toml in Xenia's folder (build e6cd2e4's default while it names
none) and written one value at a time in Xenia's own layout, the rest kept, never while Xenia runs
(emulator.running, new). The wiki says so.

Changelog: 03-11-2026 21:47:23

Added. A game renamed or moved after it was put in Steam keeps its mark when the app can tell it is the same game
(its code, else its file's size; core's renamed, the app's settings remember what each game in Steam is): Refresh,
or the next start, shows it under its new name, ticked and said so under the tabs, and Update Steam puts it in
Steam under that name and takes the old shortcut out (owner, 03-11-2026, from the Windows Portable Suite's managers,
01-11-2026). A shortcut to a game that is no longer there no longer starts Xenia with a file that is not
there: the run wrapper says so and ends with 1, and shows a message box of the app's own (--gone, core's gone),
which closes by itself, so Steam sees the game end. The wiki says so.

Changelog: 03-11-2026 21:37:27

Added. Remove game… on Your games (owner, 03-11-2026, from the Windows Portable Suite's managers, 30-10-2026 and
01-11-2026: a game that no longer plays goes, files and all, and before deleting anything the user decides what to
keep; core's keep and keep_dialog): a window lists what of the chosen game would go, a row each with its size, every
row ticked; unticking a row keeps it, Delete marked deletes the rows still ticked off the window's thread (read-only
files too) and takes its Steam shortcut out through Steam when that row is ticked, and Cancel deletes nothing
(library.removal_items(); Xenia's content folder, with the saves never among the rows). A game the app will not delete is said so.
The wiki says so.

Changelog: 03-11-2026 21:17:50

Breaking. No folder is chosen or browsed to any more (owner, 03-11-2026, from the Windows Portable Suite's Xenia
Manager, 30-10-2026: fixed folders, no folder selecting): the buttons Add folder… and Remove folder…, with their
windows, are gone, and the folders added before are no longer looked in (the settings' folders key is dropped;
library.py). Added. The app's own game folder: ~/Games/XBOX360, made when the window opens, and Games/XBOX360 on each
removable drive that has one (mounted under /run/media or /media; core's drives), always looked in
(library.fixed()). The Game folder line names the folders (the home folder as ~). The wiki has a chapter for it,
Where your games go.

Changelog: 03-11-2026 21:04:45

Fixed. Update Steam reads Steam's file back right after writing it, while Steam is still closed, and says on the
status line and in the output when a game it wrote is not found there, by name (owner, 03-11-2026, from the Windows
Portable Suite's managers, 29-10-2026: "it still says 0 games in Steam"), so the message tells whether the file or
the reading is at fault; a failed read of the file is said too instead of passed over. Nothing changes when the
shortcuts read back as written.

Changelog: 03-11-2026 20:54:32

Fixed. No user name on the screen or in the log (owner, 03-11-2026: the suite's privacy rule, as the Windows Portable
Suite's apps keep it since 29-10-2026): the game folders on the first step, and every message under the tabs and in the output show your home folder as ~ (core's platform.private).

